# bat's own config, and the SINGLE place the theme is set.
#
# BAT_THEME used to be exported from three places as well -- .bashrc,
# environment.d/apps.conf and conf.d/00-env.fish -- and they disagreed: bash got
# "Catppuccin Mocha" while fish got "ansi". The env var wins over this file, so
# fish sessions rendered flat 4-bit ANSI while the repo shipped and tracked a
# Catppuccin theme nobody saw. Those exports are gone; bat reads this file
# natively, so there is nothing left to drift against.
--theme="Catppuccin Mocha"
--style="full"
--paging="auto"
--map-syntax "*.conf:INI"
--map-syntax "*.service:INI"
--map-syntax "*.mount:INI"